 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Use",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "An NPN transistor for high-voltage switching and amplification, including telephony. One type, CXT5551, in SOT-89, marked 1G6 on the body."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gain against current and temperature",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "At VCE = 5 V the gain at 25 °C rises from about 137 at 0.3 mA to a broad peak near 157 around 14 to 24 mA, then falls steeply above about 50 mA to about 34 at 200 mA. At 100 °C it starts near 223, peaks near 234 at about 6 mA and drops below the 25 °C curve beyond roughly 70 mA (Fig.2)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Saturation",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "With base current one tenth of the collector current, VCE(sat) is about 85 to 98 mV at 0.1 mA, dips to about 49 to 55 mV between 5 and 9 mA, and climbs to roughly 400 to 520 mV at 300 mA, higher at 100 °C than at -25 °C (Fig.3). VBE(sat) under the same drive runs from about 381 mV (100 °C) and 558 mV (-25 °C) at 0.1 mA to about 840 and 925 mV near 300 mA (Fig.4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output characteristic",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "In common emitter at 25 °C, base current steps of 20 µA give collector currents from about 4 mA (20 µA) to about 32 mA (200 µA) once VCE passes a few volts, with a slight upward slope with VCE (Fig.1)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The SOT-89 body is moulded in compound rated UL 94V-0, RoHS compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. Moisture sensitivity level 1 to J-STD-020, with a lead-free reflow peak of 260 °C."
  }
 ],
